  "unit": "Unit 17 - Absolute Value",
  "description": "Comprehensive lesson covering Unit 17 - Absolute Value for SAT Math preparation.",
  "duration": 45,
  "content": "<p><strong>Unit 17 - Absolute Value — Title &amp; Goal</strong><br />Comprehensive lesson covering Unit 17 - Absolute Value for SAT Math preparation.</p>\n\n\n<h3>Key idea</h3>\n<p>Read the idea and scan the rules. Focus on how the symbols behave.</p>\n<ol>\n<li><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math> (always nonnegative).  </li>\n<li><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo></mrow></math>.  </li>\n<li><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo></mrow></math>.  </li>\n<li><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mrow><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"prefix\" stretchy=\"true\">|</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>a</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo fence=\"true\" form=\"postfix\" stretchy=\"true\">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><mi>b</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math>.  </li>\n<li>Triangle inequality: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mo>≤</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo></mrow></math>.  </li>\n</ol>\n<hr/>\n<h3>Next idea</h3><p>Build on the previous idea. Notice what changes and what stays the same.</p><p><strong>Case 1: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></math></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>If <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math>: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></math> or <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></math>.  </li>\n<li>If <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math>: No solution.  </li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Worked example</h3>\n<p>Follow the steps carefully, then try to reproduce them without looking.</p>\n<p><strong>Example 1</strong><br/>\nSolve <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></math>.  </p>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mtext>or</mtext><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></math>\n<h3>Quick practice</h3>\n<p>Try these on your own. Check your steps, not just the final answer.</p>\n<p>1) Solve <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow></math>.\n2) Solve <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math>.\n3) Solve <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mo>≤</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></math>.\n<h3>Next idea</h3>\n<p>Build on the previous idea. Notice what changes and what stays the same.</p>\n<hr/>\n<h3>Next idea</h3><p>Build on the previous idea. Notice what changes and what stays the same.</p><p><strong>Case 2: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></math></strong></p>\n<p>Split into two cases.  </p>\n<h3>Another example</h3>\n<p>Compare this approach to the previous one. What’s the same? What’s different?</p>\n<p><strong>Example 2</strong><br/>\nSolve <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></math>.  </p>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mo>⇒</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></math>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mo>⇒</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></math>\n<hr/>\n<ol>\n<li><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>a</mi><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><mo>⇒</mo><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></math> </li>\n<li><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mo>≤</mo><mi>a</mi><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><mo>⇒</mo><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></math> </li>\n<li><math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>a</mi><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><mo>⇒</mo><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><mspace width=\"0.278em\"></mspace><mi>x</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></math> or <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></math> </li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>Example 3</strong><br/>\nSolve <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></math>.  </p>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>3</mn><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mo>⇒</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mn>1</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></math>\n<p><strong>Example 4</strong><br/>\nSolve <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mo>≥</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></math>.  </p>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>≥</mo><mn>5</mn><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mo>⇒</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mi>x</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></math>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mo>⇒</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mi>x</mi><mo>≤</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></math>\n<hr/>\n<p>Distance is always nonnegative.  </p>\n<p><strong>Example 5</strong><br/>\nA number is within 4 units of 10. Find the range of possible values.  </p>\n<p>Equation: <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>10</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mo>≤</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></math>.  </p>\n<math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>14</mn></mrow></math>\n<hr/>\n<ul>\n<li>Always split into cases.  </li>\n<li>Check for <strong>no solutions</strong> when RHS is negative.  </li>\n<li>Graph inequalities on number line if unsure.  </li>\n<li>Remember: absolute value = distance.  </li>\n</ul>\n<hr/>\n<p>1) Solve <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow></math>.<br/>\n2) Solve <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></math>.<br/>\n3) Solve <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mo>≤</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></math>.<br/>\n4) Solve <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></math>.<br/>\n5) A number is within 2 units of <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></math>. Write inequality and solution set.  </p>\n<hr/>\n<p>1) <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow></math> or <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow></math>.  </p>\n<p>2) <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></math>.  </p>\n<p>3) <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>≤</mo><mn>6</mn><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mo>⇒</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></math>.  </p>\n<p>4) <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>10</mn><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mo>⇒</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mi>x</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></math><br/>\n   OR <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>10</mn><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mo>⇒</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mi>x</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>14</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></math>.  </p>\n<p>5) <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mo>⇒</mo><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mo>−</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>≤</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></math>.  </p>\n<h3>More practice</h3>\n<p>Keep going—aim for accuracy first, then speed.</p>\n<h3>Mixed practice set</h3>\n<p>These mix everything above. Time yourself and reflect on any mistakes.</p>\n4) Solve <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></math>.\n5) A number is within 2 units of <math display=\"inline\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></math>. Write inequality and solution set.",
